    "q-112257": {
      "dom_id": "step-q112257",
      "name": "Question 2",
      "problem": "A social media influencer had $100$ followers the day she created her account. Since then, the number $F(t)$ of followers after $t$ weeks can be modeled by the function\n\n$$\nF(t)=100\\cdot {3}^{t}.\n$$\n\nHow many weeks will it take for the followers to increase to $72\\,900?$",
      "worked_solution": "To find the time it takes for the number of followers to increase to $72\\,900,$ we need to solve the equation $F(t)=72\\,900$ for $t,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(t) & =72\\,900 \\\\ 100\\cdot {3}^{t} & =72\\,900 \\\\ {3}^{t} & =\\frac{72\\,900}{100} \\\\ {3}^{t} & =729 \\\\ {3}^{t} & ={3}^{6} \\\\ t & =6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the number of followers increases to $72\\,900$ after $6$ weeks.",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
