    "q-112316": {
      "dom_id": "step-q112316",
      "name": "Question 8",
      "problem": "The profits of a store $P(t),$ $t$ years after $2018,$ is given by\n\n$$\nP(t)={P}_{0}\\cdot (1.1)^{t},\n$$\n\nwhere ${P}_{0}$ was the profit in $2018.$ If the profits in $2020$ were of $$48\\,400,$ what was the profit in $2018?$",
      "worked_solution": "The store profits in $2020$ were of $$48\\,400,$ this is $2$ years after $2018.$ Thus, $P(2)=48\\,400.$\n\nTo find the profit ${P}_{0}$ in $2018,$  we substitute $t=2$ and $P(2)=48\\,400$ into the given equation and solve for ${P}_{0},$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(2) & ={P}_{0}\\cdot (1.1)^{2} \\\\ 48\\,400 & ={P}_{0}\\cdot (1.1)^{2} \\\\ {P}_{0} & =\\frac{48\\,400}{1.21} \\\\ {P}_{0} & =40\\,000\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the profits in $2018$ were of $$40\\,000.$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
